WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.380
What is NP, and how

2
00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:03.240
do you write a verifier

3
00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:05.800
proof? A yes instance must

4
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.300
have a certificate of polynomial

5
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.620
encoded length that a deterministic

6
00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:13.020
polynomial-time verifier accepts. A no

7
00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:14.780
instance must make every allowed

8
00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:17.020
certificate fail, so a convincing

9
00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:18.500
example alone is not enough.

10
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:21.560
This is equivalent to polynomial-time

11
00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:25.580
nondeterministic computation. One direction records

12
00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:27.340
an accepting machine’s choices as

13
00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.360
a certificate and simulates them

14
00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.840
deterministically. The other guesses a

15
00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.240
polynomial-length certificate and runs the

16
00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.640
verifier, with every branch obeying

17
00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.140
a polynomial time bound.

18
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.480
Consider the Vertex Cover decision

19
00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:42.500
language: a graph and integer

20
00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:43.960
k asking for a cover

21
00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.340
of size at most k.

22
00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:47.140
A certificate can be one

23
00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:49.280
selection bit per vertex. The

24
00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.440
verifier counts selected vertices and

25
00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:52.900
checks that every edge has

26
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:54.380
at least one selected endpoint.

27
00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:56.040
If the graph has a

28
00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:58.220
suitable cover, its selection mask

29
00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:00.500
passes all checks. If a

30
00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:02.320
mask passes, the size bound

31
00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:03.900
and edge checks prove that

32
00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:05.000
it really is a suitable

33
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.300
cover, so no no-instance can

34
00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.300
fool the verifier. The mask

35
00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.100
length and all explicit graph

36
00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.680
checks are polynomial in the

37
00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:13.380
input encoding.

38
00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:16.180
For Independent Set or Clique,

39
00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:18.240
give a vertex subset and

40
00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:19.880
check its cardinality and all

41
00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:22.540
selected pairs. Independent Set forbids

42
00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:24.660
every internal edge, while Clique

43
00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:26.120
requires every pair to have

44
00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:27.640
an edge. A proof that

45
00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:28.900
checks only a few listed

46
00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:30.800
edges does not verify the

47
00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:31.880
universal pair condition.

48
00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:34.760
For a Hamiltonian cycle, the

49
00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:36.500
certificate is an ordering of

50
00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:39.580
all vertices. Verify valid names,

51
00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:43.080
no repetitions, complete coverage, every

52
00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.080
consecutive edge and the closing

53
00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:46.280
edge back to the start.

54
00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:48.940
A path verifier omits cycle

55
00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:52.140
closure, while a longest-simple-path verifier

56
00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:54.660
must also enforce distinct vertices

57
00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:57.000
and the requested length threshold.

58
00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:00.080
For SAT, a truth assignment

59
00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:02.400
is the certificate and evaluating

60
00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.840
all clauses is polynomial in

61
00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:07.020
the formula length. For Subset

62
00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:08.880
Sum, use a bit mask

63
00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:11.260
selecting input indices and check

64
00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:12.820
the binary sum against the

65
00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:15.580
target. Repeated equal values still

66
00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:18.620
occupy different indices, and polynomially

67
00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:20.820
many additions keep polynomial bit

68
00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:21.120
lengths.

69
00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:23.620
A verifier need not find

70
00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:26.520
the certificate efficiently. NP membership

71
00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:28.120
asserts that a suitable short

72
00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:29.840
witness exists and can be

73
00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:31.720
checked, not that searching for

74
00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:33.120
it is already known polynomial.

75
00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:36.920
Likewise, NP means nondeterministic polynomial

76
00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:39.300
time, not non-polynomial time.

77
00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:42.360
Deterministic polynomial algorithms are a

78
00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.460
special case of nondeterministic ones,

79
00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:46.440
giving P contained in NP.

80
00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.760
Enumerating all polynomial-size certificates gives

81
00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:52.440
an exponential deterministic bound, placing

82
00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:55.080
NP within EXP. The known

83
00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:57.120
separation of P from EXP

84
00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:58.760
does not decide which intermediate

85
00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:00.580
inclusion is strict or settle

86
00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:01.740
P versus NP.

87
00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:04.020
Things to take note of.

88
00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:07.100
Specify the decision language, certificate

89
00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:09.640
encoding, length bound, all verifier

90
00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:11.680
checks and a polynomial bit-time

91
00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:14.700
analysis. Explain both why genuine

92
00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:16.360
yes instances have a passing

93
00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:18.360
certificate and why no instance

94
00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.500
can pass; the phrase easy

95
00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:21.580
to check is only the

96
00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:22.520
beginning of the proof.
